# GitHub — egress this entry needs.
#
# Allowlist syntax, so what you read here is what lands in the deployment's
# /etc/agent-allowlist. Uncommented lines are what the provider needs to work;
# anything below the OPTIONAL marker is off until you turn it on.
#
# METHODS is not optional in practice. Omitting it defaults the entry to
# GET,HEAD,OPTIONS, so a bare `api.github.com` line leaves every `gh` write
# denied while looking right.

api.github.com          GET,POST,PATCH,PUT,DELETE
uploads.github.com      POST
github.com              *

# github.com is here and is NOT in the entry's `hosts`, which is the clearest
# case in the bank of those being two different lists. This entry ships a git
# credential helper (lab/setup-github.sh), so git push/pull over HTTPS is part
# of what installing it gives you — and that traffic must be able to leave.
# What it must never do is go through 010_github.py: git runs its own Basic-auth
# handshake inside the tunnel, which an injected Authorization header breaks.
# So: reachable, deliberately not credentialed. `*` because git fetch is GET and
# git push is POST to the same host.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — nothing below is needed for the provider to work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# codeload.github.com             GET     # tarball/zipball downloads, `gh repo archive`
# objects.githubusercontent.com   GET     # release assets and git-LFS objects
# raw.githubusercontent.com       GET     # raw file fetches outside the API
